  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A 2.0 Ω and a 4.0 Ω resistor are connected in parallel to a cell with negligible internal resistance. An ammeter placed in the circuit as shown measures a current of 1.0 A.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>What is the current passing through the 2.0 Ω resistor?<br/><br/></p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">0.5 A</li><li data-label=\"B\">1.0 A</li><li data-label=\"C\">2.0 A</li><li data-label=\"D\">4.0 A</li></ol>"
